1
00:00:14,681 --> 00:00:19,184
<i>My hero, the legendary hit man
Mr. Sakamoto,</i>

2
00:00:19,185 --> 00:00:21,688
<i>fell in love
and retired from his life of crime.</i>

3
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:28,653
<i>All he wanted was the quiet warmth
of living a normal life.</i>

4
00:00:29,362 --> 00:00:34,158
<i>But the JAA was relentless,
sending assassin after assassin after him.</i>

5
00:00:34,159 --> 00:00:35,492
<i>Apparently, someone called Slur</i>

6
00:00:35,493 --> 00:00:39,413
<i>put a bounty of one billion yen
on Mr. Sakamoto's head.</i>

7
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:40,706
<i>Screw them!</i>

8
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:44,877
<i>If that wasn't bad enough, Slur brought
a group of violent criminals to Japan</i>

9
00:00:44,878 --> 00:00:49,507
<i>and is trying to ruin
Mr. Sakamoto's precious normal life.</i>

10
00:00:50,175 --> 00:00:52,843
<i>But we won't let him get the best of us!</i>

11
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:54,345
LU - SHIN - SAKAMOTO

12
00:01:23,124 --> 00:01:25,042
Please... Let me go!

13
00:01:25,043 --> 00:01:26,294
Why are you after me?

14
00:01:27,045 --> 00:01:28,379
Who the hell are you?!

15
00:01:29,005 --> 00:01:30,673
You look scared.

16
00:01:37,639 --> 00:01:39,224
How cute.

17
00:01:41,476 --> 00:01:42,602
I like you.

18
00:01:49,818 --> 00:01:50,985
Wait...

19
00:01:54,197 --> 00:01:55,156
Was this guy

20
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:57,242
always so ugly?

21
00:01:57,742 --> 00:02:00,662
He was so cute just now.

22
00:02:02,997 --> 00:02:04,832
I guess nothing's cuter

23
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:08,670
than that terrified look people get
right before they die.

24
00:02:10,213 --> 00:02:12,465
But every time I see that look,

25
00:02:13,424 --> 00:02:16,177
I get too excited and end up killing them.

26
00:02:17,303 --> 00:02:19,597
I should work on my self-control.

27
00:02:20,098 --> 00:02:21,933
{\an8}DUMP
DEATH ROW INMATE

28
00:02:24,978 --> 00:02:27,730
This is perfect. Tomorrow's job
will go off without a hitch.

29
00:02:30,567 --> 00:02:31,442
Who's there?!

30
00:02:34,028 --> 00:02:35,738
Wait... What?

31
00:02:46,249 --> 00:02:49,210
I finally understand you now.

32
00:02:49,919 --> 00:02:53,046
It really is
what's on the inside that counts!

33
00:02:53,047 --> 00:02:55,049
Oh?

34
00:02:56,593 --> 00:02:58,845
Volume 7 is missing.

35
00:02:59,721 --> 00:03:01,096
That's not right.

36
00:03:01,097 --> 00:03:03,015
Not right. Not right. Not right.

37
00:03:03,016 --> 00:03:06,477
Not right, not right, not right!

38
00:03:08,354 --> 00:03:09,480
I'll take this.

39
00:03:11,441 --> 00:03:13,109
That'll be 484 yen.

40
00:03:15,486 --> 00:03:16,487
That's better!

41
00:03:17,196 --> 00:03:18,907
{\an8}APART
DEATH ROW INMATE

42
00:03:22,493 --> 00:03:24,245
I need more...

43
00:03:24,746 --> 00:03:27,540
This isn't nearly enough for me.

44
00:03:30,543 --> 00:03:33,503
Where are those S-rank whatevers?

45
00:03:33,504 --> 00:03:35,131
{\an8}MINIMALIST
DEATH ROW INMATE

46
00:03:36,799 --> 00:03:37,883
KILLED THREE D-RANKS

47
00:03:37,884 --> 00:03:38,967
I GOT ONE B-RANK

48
00:03:38,968 --> 00:03:40,552
Whoa, whoa!

49
00:03:40,553 --> 00:03:43,055
I know we haven't killed in a while,
but cool your jets.

50
00:03:43,056 --> 00:03:44,056
THAT WAS FAST LOL

51
00:03:44,057 --> 00:03:46,726
Rushing into things is so uncool.

52
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:49,520
{\an8}What are you doing? Working?

53
00:03:50,021 --> 00:03:52,649
Yeah. Just go back to bed.

54
00:03:53,524 --> 00:03:54,817
Such a waste.

55
00:03:55,401 --> 00:03:59,696
Knowing their personality, their history,
all their stories is what makes

56
00:03:59,697 --> 00:04:01,365
seeing their ending so exciting.

57
00:04:01,366 --> 00:04:02,449
SAW
DEATH ROW INMATE

58
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:07,705
Now... Whose ending
would be the most entertaining?

59
00:05:41,257 --> 00:05:43,926
{\an8}<i>Sakamoto, I am entrusting my lady to you.</i>

60
00:05:44,510 --> 00:05:47,346
{\an8}<i>I will continue looking into Slur.</i>

61
00:05:48,014 --> 00:05:50,558
<i>Those death row inmates are out there.
Be careful.</i>

62
00:05:51,142 --> 00:05:52,685
<i>They murder for the fun of it.</i>

63
00:05:53,227 --> 00:05:55,980
<i>They're a different breed
from hit men and mafia thugs.</i>

64
00:05:58,399 --> 00:06:01,026
{\an8}I'm surprised Wutang left
without much of a fuss.

65
00:06:01,027 --> 00:06:04,071
{\an8}Yeah, but that jerk
took all the money we won.

66
00:06:04,072 --> 00:06:04,988
VIDEO RENTALS

67
00:06:04,989 --> 00:06:08,534
First things first.
We need intel on the enemy.

68
00:06:12,997 --> 00:06:14,540
Hello, Mr. Sakamoto.

69
00:06:15,124 --> 00:06:17,585
What can I help you find today?

70
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:22,256
I want to know about the death row inmate
murders from the other day.

71
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:25,509
That'll be under "psycho horror."

72
00:06:25,510 --> 00:06:29,012
{\an8}HUMAN LIZARD - DON'T PLEASE - SLEEPY FISH
MAD SOMMAR - THE SILENCE OF THE GOATS

73
00:06:29,013 --> 00:06:30,972
Oh, this looks good.

74
00:06:30,973 --> 00:06:33,433
Everything here is R-rated.

75
00:06:33,434 --> 00:06:34,601
{\an8}TECHNICAL CHAINSAW MASSACRE

76
00:06:34,602 --> 00:06:36,311
{\an8}We need all the intel we can get!

77
00:06:36,312 --> 00:06:38,980
Can I close my eyes if I get scared?

78
00:06:38,981 --> 00:06:41,775
- That'll be 1,083,000 yen.
- You don't get to slack off.

79
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:43,860
- I really can't do horror...
- Credit.

80
00:06:43,861 --> 00:06:45,321
- You're hopeless.
- Thank you.

81
00:06:49,617 --> 00:06:50,826
Have you heard?

82
00:06:50,827 --> 00:06:55,580
A gang of crooks has been causing trouble
the past few days.

83
00:06:55,581 --> 00:06:59,417
Oh, no. They sound real scary.

84
00:06:59,418 --> 00:07:01,587
Look at you, frothing at the mouth.

85
00:07:06,968 --> 00:07:09,679
Osaragi, this is the wrong way.

86
00:07:10,179 --> 00:07:11,973
I missed the turn.

87
00:07:13,516 --> 00:07:15,309
Let me back up.

88
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:18,061
All clear!

89
00:07:18,062 --> 00:07:21,023
We're on the highway,
you can't just reverse.

90
00:07:21,566 --> 00:07:24,152
But I must say,
you look good in the driver's seat.

91
00:07:27,155 --> 00:07:28,655
Dammit, Osaragi!

92
00:07:28,656 --> 00:07:30,658
Can't you drive more carefully?

93
00:07:31,159 --> 00:07:32,869
There's a senior citizen in here!

94
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:35,036
I'm sorry.

95
00:07:35,037 --> 00:07:37,290
Mr. Shishiba made me drive.

96
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:40,376
Both hands on the wheel, Osaragi.

97
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:46,466
Anyway, I don't care
if they're on death row or not.

98
00:07:46,966 --> 00:07:49,468
{\an8}You mess around on our turf,
you're dead meat.

99
00:07:49,469 --> 00:07:50,385
{\an8}HYO
THE ORDER

100
00:07:50,386 --> 00:07:55,558
That line's from a movie I saw yesterday!
One of the thugs said it before he died.

101
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:57,559
- You saw it too, Hyo?
- What?

102
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:58,477
{\an8}NAGUMO
THE ORDER

103
00:07:58,478 --> 00:08:01,396
{\an8}Give it a rest, Nagumo. Don't stir him up.

104
00:08:01,397 --> 00:08:02,314
{\an8}SHISHIBA
THE ORDER

105
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:03,816
{\an8}Whatever do you mean?

106
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:09,779
Osaragi, use your indicator.

107
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:11,448
{\an8}I was about to.

108
00:08:11,449 --> 00:08:12,365
{\an8}OSARAGI
THE ORDER

109
00:08:12,366 --> 00:08:16,329
{\an8}Well, they may be crazed murderers,
but they're amateurs, aren't they?

110
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:19,080
What is Slur thinking?

111
00:08:19,081 --> 00:08:20,832
I don't understand one bit.

112
00:08:20,833 --> 00:08:24,252
Without any morals or even a conscience,

113
00:08:24,253 --> 00:08:26,713
when it comes to killing,
they have no brakes.

114
00:08:26,714 --> 00:08:28,840
That might make them tougher
than they seem.

115
00:08:28,841 --> 00:08:31,551
When it comes to killing,
you've got no brakes either.

116
00:08:31,552 --> 00:08:32,637
I do too.

117
00:08:39,435 --> 00:08:40,769
{\an8}Hey!

118
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:42,188
Osaragi, get down!

119
00:08:56,327 --> 00:08:59,746
We've got another one here.
A killer with no brakes.

120
00:08:59,747 --> 00:09:02,374
He's got his pedal to the metal.

121
00:09:02,375 --> 00:09:03,960
That's Mr. Takamura for you.

122
00:09:05,002 --> 00:09:06,253
{\an8}TAKAMURA
THE ORDER

123
00:09:06,254 --> 00:09:08,506
- What was that?
- What happened?

124
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:11,925
In any case, there are four of them, so...

125
00:09:11,926 --> 00:09:15,011
{\an8}We have more than enough to take them on.

126
00:09:15,012 --> 00:09:17,722
Mr. Shishiba,
we should eat <i>tonkatsu</i> for good luck.

127
00:09:17,723 --> 00:09:19,684
I forgot how superstitious you are.

128
00:09:23,312 --> 00:09:25,606
<i>Get away! Stop it!</i>

129
00:09:30,069 --> 00:09:31,987
Hey, he fell asleep!

130
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:35,575
This isn't scary, it's just gross.

131
00:09:59,557 --> 00:10:02,434
Whoa! That was awesome, Taro!

132
00:10:02,435 --> 00:10:06,063
You caught 99 shots in a row!

133
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:07,857
<i>Missed one.</i>

134
00:10:08,357 --> 00:10:10,276
But man,

135
00:10:10,943 --> 00:10:12,902
training with you one-on-one is so fun.

136
00:10:12,903 --> 00:10:15,531
It's like we're real pals!

137
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:19,702
Heisuke, give me one more shot
while there's no one else around.

138
00:10:20,202 --> 00:10:22,537
You really are amazing, huh, Mr. Sakamoto?

139
00:10:22,538 --> 00:10:24,247
{\an8}Hey, Shin!

140
00:10:24,248 --> 00:10:27,418
{\an8}But no matter how hard you train,

141
00:10:28,085 --> 00:10:29,754
if you die, you die.

142
00:10:34,717 --> 00:10:37,053
What do you want, Nagumo?

143
00:10:37,970 --> 00:10:39,888
You saw right through me.

144
00:10:39,889 --> 00:10:44,142
What?! Shin, your vibe is way different
than it was a minute ago.

145
00:10:44,143 --> 00:10:46,061
- I heard, Sakamoto.
- Did you get a makeover?

146
00:10:46,062 --> 00:10:50,148
- You're looking fresh!
- You've been snooping around

147
00:10:50,149 --> 00:10:51,608
about Slur's death row inmates.

148
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:53,277
What if I was?

149
00:10:53,778 --> 00:10:56,280
The Order is already on it.

150
00:10:56,781 --> 00:10:59,282
Lowly mom-and-pop shop workers
should stay out of it.

151
00:10:59,283 --> 00:11:02,536
No thanks.
Waiting around won't do any good.

152
00:11:03,162 --> 00:11:05,789
I'm giving you this warning as a friend.

153
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:09,210
You've been ordered to kill them all,
haven't you?

154
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:12,254
I want information on Slur,

155
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:15,299
so I need to get to them
before The Order does.

156
00:11:15,925 --> 00:11:17,927
{\an8}You mean you're going to take them alive?

157
00:11:18,427 --> 00:11:20,179
{\an8}You're as soft as ever.

158
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:25,059
Let me clue you in
on what your enemies make of you.

159
00:11:29,772 --> 00:11:30,981
The heck is this?

160
00:11:31,649 --> 00:11:33,108
Rank B.

161
00:11:33,109 --> 00:11:35,236
It means you're easy prey.

162
00:11:36,487 --> 00:11:37,655
In case you're wondering,

163
00:11:38,155 --> 00:11:40,366
they put me at rank S.

164
00:11:42,493 --> 00:11:44,412
SUZUKI
HOME IMPROVEMENT STORE

165
00:11:46,997 --> 00:11:50,542
Aww, this kitty's so cute!

166
00:11:50,543 --> 00:11:52,920
Come on, let's grab what we need
and get out.

167
00:11:53,462 --> 00:11:54,921
What are we buying?

168
00:11:54,922 --> 00:11:57,216
Stuff to fix the shop's exterior.

169
00:11:58,008 --> 00:12:01,762
For some reason,
I keep finding holes in the walls lately.

170
00:12:04,306 --> 00:12:06,224
Just a few more minutes!

171
00:12:06,225 --> 00:12:08,852
What's the big rush?

172
00:12:08,853 --> 00:12:10,813
Wish I could be as carefree as you.

173
00:12:12,189 --> 00:12:14,650
Those dangerous death row inmates
are on the prowl.

174
00:12:15,234 --> 00:12:16,652
You saw the videos yourself.

175
00:12:17,194 --> 00:12:19,654
Mr. Manager is strong, so we'll be fine.

176
00:12:19,655 --> 00:12:21,323
That's not the point...

177
00:12:21,824 --> 00:12:26,036
{\an8}Seriously, right now we're nothing
but a burden to Mr. Sakamoto.

178
00:12:27,037 --> 00:12:28,955
<i>If we want to be by his side,</i>

179
00:12:28,956 --> 00:12:30,624
<i>we have to get better.</i>

180
00:12:31,417 --> 00:12:34,503
{\an8}We have to get stronger too.

181
00:12:36,172 --> 00:12:37,297
Listen to me!

182
00:12:37,298 --> 00:12:39,675
Would you like to hold one too?

183
00:12:40,718 --> 00:12:41,635
I'm in a hurry.

184
00:12:42,636 --> 00:12:44,512
But look how cute he is!

185
00:12:44,513 --> 00:12:46,682
I'm not interested in dogs!

186
00:12:48,476 --> 00:12:49,768
{\an8}MOCHI
SHIBA INU

187
00:12:52,563 --> 00:12:54,023
What a cutie you are!

188
00:12:56,358 --> 00:12:58,568
Shin, let's get going already.

189
00:12:58,569 --> 00:13:01,322
Aww, just a few more minutes!

190
00:13:03,657 --> 00:13:07,286
- What's the matter? You need to pee?
- That's not what having to pee looks like!

191
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:13,501
What's going on?

192
00:13:14,668 --> 00:13:15,794
You idiots.

193
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:21,299
Not very smart to start howling
when you run into a shady character.

194
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:24,802
{\an8}What you should do is tuck your tail
between your legs and run.

195
00:13:24,803 --> 00:13:27,305
Who're you, old man?

196
00:13:27,306 --> 00:13:30,225
I'm ex-military, you know?

197
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:33,562
I've seen plenty of people bite it
because they made the wrong choice.

198
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:36,397
{\an8}Such a shame.

199
00:13:36,398 --> 00:13:39,985
{\an8}Everyone deserves to have
a dramatic ending.

200
00:13:40,569 --> 00:13:42,654
So I've made some special arrangements

201
00:13:42,655 --> 00:13:46,534
to give everyone a truly moving ending.

202
00:13:49,119 --> 00:13:55,125
First, I'll kill that fatty's
family and friends and make him despair.

203
00:13:59,338 --> 00:14:00,339
Shin!

204
00:14:02,967 --> 00:14:05,427
I hate to waste time
on the side-characters.

205
00:14:06,387 --> 00:14:08,639
It gets boring
if you don't keep the pace up.

206
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:19,065
Shin, this guy...

207
00:14:19,066 --> 00:14:22,318
Definitely. He's one of
the death row inmates.

208
00:14:22,319 --> 00:14:25,823
Not bad. I thought I cut you clean in two,

209
00:14:26,532 --> 00:14:29,451
<i>but you used that crowbar
to block at the last second, huh?</i>

210
00:14:30,411 --> 00:14:32,871
Good move, Shin.

211
00:14:32,872 --> 00:14:36,457
Screw you. How do you know my name?

212
00:14:36,458 --> 00:14:39,420
All the targets' info is right here.

213
00:14:40,462 --> 00:14:44,633
The only child of the Lu clan,
Lu Shaotang. Rank C.

214
00:14:45,634 --> 00:14:49,930
Ex-hit man and psychic, Shin. Rank D.

215
00:14:52,141 --> 00:14:54,225
Hey! Wait just one minute!

216
00:14:54,226 --> 00:14:56,811
You mean my rank is lower than Lu's?!

217
00:14:56,812 --> 00:14:58,146
I mean, look.

218
00:14:58,147 --> 00:15:00,773
FYI, D is the second-lowest rank.

219
00:15:00,774 --> 00:15:04,569
How can this be? She's just a drunkard!

220
00:15:04,570 --> 00:15:05,904
Shut up!

221
00:15:05,905 --> 00:15:08,573
Don't get too down in the dumps, Shin.

222
00:15:08,574 --> 00:15:11,911
Everyone gets an ending, even D-ranks.

223
00:15:14,371 --> 00:15:15,539
{\an8}D, huh.

224
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,250
Hey!

225
00:15:19,251 --> 00:15:21,670
<i>I'll go for a clean cut
right through his waist!</i>

226
00:15:33,015 --> 00:15:37,477
You can fix my ranking
after I beat you half to death,

227
00:15:37,478 --> 00:15:39,563
you psychotic murder-obsessed bastard!

228
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:42,607
Hey now, you've hurt my feelings.

229
00:15:42,608 --> 00:15:45,151
You make me sound
like some scary murderer.

230
00:15:45,152 --> 00:15:48,655
Well, you've murdered a bunch of people!

231
00:15:48,656 --> 00:15:51,450
I'm sure everyone I killed appreciated it.

232
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:54,827
Even in the crappiest movies or comics,

233
00:15:54,828 --> 00:15:58,665
if there's an exciting twist
or a dramatic moment at the end,

234
00:15:58,666 --> 00:16:02,752
you come away feeling entertained,
don't you?

235
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:04,963
{\an8}It's the same with people.

236
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:07,590
{\an8}I feel bad for the ones
who live a boring life.

237
00:16:07,591 --> 00:16:11,929
So, as a present,
I give them the best ending possible.

238
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:14,682
Don't worry.

239
00:16:16,183 --> 00:16:20,229
I'll make sure your lives
are super entertaining.

240
00:16:21,313 --> 00:16:23,732
<i>What the hell? This guy's thoughts...</i>

241
00:16:30,948 --> 00:16:32,408
Are you all right? Lu!

242
00:16:33,033 --> 00:16:33,909
Yeah...

243
00:16:35,369 --> 00:16:37,662
Come on, keep up the good fight.

244
00:16:37,663 --> 00:16:38,872
This is bad!

245
00:16:49,299 --> 00:16:51,676
Can't you tell
where he's about to throw it?!

246
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:54,221
All I can hear is him thinking "kill"!

247
00:16:54,847 --> 00:16:57,056
We have to find
something to fight back with!

248
00:16:57,057 --> 00:17:00,060
What about a hammer? Or a shovel?

249
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:04,481
Watch out!

250
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:12,197
I heard you were a psychic, Shin.

251
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:16,201
My thoughts right now
are super clear, aren't they?

252
00:17:17,369 --> 00:17:20,204
When there are boring losers like you
in front of me,

253
00:17:20,205 --> 00:17:23,959
all I can think about is killing them.

254
00:17:27,129 --> 00:17:28,881
Get away from Shin!

255
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:33,886
A nail gun, eh? I like you.

256
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:36,263
LACQUER SPRAY

257
00:17:42,644 --> 00:17:43,812
Did we get him?

258
00:17:46,523 --> 00:17:48,817
You guys are fun.

259
00:17:49,318 --> 00:17:51,611
The more you struggle,
the more you fight back,

260
00:17:51,612 --> 00:17:55,114
the more moving your endings will be.

261
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:57,700
<i>This guy just won't back down!</i>

262
00:17:57,701 --> 00:17:59,703
<i>He's beyond tough!</i>

263
00:18:02,289 --> 00:18:03,289
NO OPEN FLAMES

264
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:04,208
Shit--

265
00:18:14,635 --> 00:18:15,676
ETHANOL

266
00:18:15,677 --> 00:18:19,139
It's important
to disinfect your wounds promptly.

267
00:18:23,227 --> 00:18:24,978
Hey... Lu!

268
00:18:26,939 --> 00:18:28,774
<i>Did she protect me?</i>

269
00:18:29,274 --> 00:18:33,194
I smell... alcohol...

270
00:18:33,195 --> 00:18:35,656
{\an8}<i>Damn it... This is all my fault!</i>

271
00:18:36,156 --> 00:18:37,699
{\an8}<i>Because I'm so weak...</i>

272
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:40,035
{\an8}<i>If I don't do something, Lu's gonna die.</i>

273
00:18:40,536 --> 00:18:42,830
{\an8}<i>What do I do? What do I do?!</i>

274
00:18:43,372 --> 00:18:44,997
{\an8}SAKAMOTO'S

275
00:18:44,998 --> 00:18:46,290
{\an8}They've been gone a while.

276
00:18:46,291 --> 00:18:47,960
You mean Shin and Lu?

277
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:50,295
I'm sure they'll be fine.

278
00:18:51,046 --> 00:18:53,966
I don't know what Shin was like
back in his hit man days,

279
00:18:54,466 --> 00:18:56,300
but he's the best!

280
00:18:56,301 --> 00:18:58,762
I mean, he's your partner, after all!

281
00:18:59,304 --> 00:19:01,473
Sure, he has potential.

282
00:19:02,015 --> 00:19:05,853
But he doesn't have much experience
with real life-or-death combat.

283
00:19:06,395 --> 00:19:08,814
I have a feeling
he still hasn't reached his ceiling.

284
00:19:10,816 --> 00:19:11,733
Oh yeah?

285
00:19:12,234 --> 00:19:13,276
Maybe.

286
00:19:13,277 --> 00:19:15,237
I don't have much experience either.

287
00:19:16,405 --> 00:19:17,781
You're a different story.

288
00:19:19,867 --> 00:19:21,951
I'm disappointed, Shin.

289
00:19:21,952 --> 00:19:23,619
Give me a little more.

290
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:25,873
Don't you feel like crying?
Or wetting yourself?

291
00:19:26,373 --> 00:19:29,876
That ability you have is fascinating.

292
00:19:29,877 --> 00:19:33,255
Too bad it went to such a boring guy.

293
00:19:33,797 --> 00:19:37,718
I'd love to be able
to peek into your head right now.

294
00:19:38,343 --> 00:19:41,805
What are you thinking about,
here, at the end of your life?

295
00:19:42,389 --> 00:19:46,101
{\an8}This is your moment.
You've got to make the most of it.

296
00:19:48,437 --> 00:19:50,271
{\an8}I'm looking forward to what comes next.

297
00:19:50,272 --> 00:19:54,484
{\an8}Once I kill you two,
Sakamoto's family is next.

298
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:58,113
I'm interested in Sakamoto.

299
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:05,162
<i>The death of a father
who's lost everything he held dear.</i>

300
00:20:06,038 --> 00:20:08,916
{\an8}That's a perfect ending, don't you think?

301
00:20:10,042 --> 00:20:14,713
I wonder what'll be going through his head
when I kill his whole family.

302
00:20:38,153 --> 00:20:39,238
<i>Mr. Sakamoto.</i>

303
00:20:43,867 --> 00:20:45,285
<i>He dodged it?</i>

304
00:20:46,078 --> 00:20:47,079
<i>What is this?</i>

305
00:20:47,579 --> 00:20:48,997
<i>Something feels off...</i>

306
00:20:52,334 --> 00:20:53,293
<i>What?</i>

307
00:20:53,877 --> 00:20:55,002
<i>How?</i>

308
00:20:55,003 --> 00:20:58,090
<i>He stopped me
before I could move my right hand.</i>

309
00:21:00,592 --> 00:21:01,801
{\an8}I can see it.

310
00:21:01,802 --> 00:21:03,262
{\an8}Your future.

311
00:21:14,564 --> 00:21:16,608
<i>What's this kid's deal?</i>

312
00:21:17,192 --> 00:21:19,778
<i>His vibe is way different
than it was a minute ago.</i>

313
00:21:25,951 --> 00:21:27,369
<i>Super reflexes...</i>

314
00:21:29,413 --> 00:21:32,666
<i>No, these aren't reflexes.</i>

315
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:36,503
<i>It's like he really can see the future!</i>

316
00:21:49,349 --> 00:21:50,892
I should thank you.

317
00:21:52,185 --> 00:21:55,397
When I was struggling
to block out your incessant thoughts,

318
00:21:55,897 --> 00:21:58,233
I found a new skill deep within myself.

319
00:21:59,901 --> 00:22:03,697
{\an8}I won't let you hurt
the people I care about!

320
00:23:32,452 --> 00:23:37,457
{\an8}Subtitle translation by: Joshua Kizuki

